sts and the convenience of its close placement to the shopping center being great positives, although countered by their çdistincté prices. Usually operating in a 24h fashion with the most luxurious room ser\vice in the whole city, the hotel is plagued with an anomaly in its structure, that takes the form of one of its rooms on the 4th floor, room 409. The entity that resides in this room consists of a multidimensional structure-like parasite, that infects bu\ildings and slowly substitutes it, with its final stage being a target structureês copy, spatially connected to a kind of hivemind in an undetermined size liminal space. A secondary characteristic of the parasite consists in consuming the target structure\ with vines and plants until they reach a ruin-like state. These plants are active and can be hostile to humans, despite not being very strong. The place can also consciously change its formation as a tactic to confuse invaders and remove any escape route\s. In the hotelês case, this specific iteration of the entity had a stunted development, becoming completely unable to expand beyond room 409, and creating a replica of the bathroom of room 404 as a facade, leading to guests thinking that the room was onl\y an employee bathroom, no longer in use, and avoiding further investigation. Its door is identical to the other ones on the floor, with the only difference being its number, 409, the only of the kind in all of the building. The plants inside are the main\ method of propagation, sticking the spores on clothing or skin of invaders that later detach in other places. The room 409 iteration, though, cannot produce spores, as its biology was permanently altered after absorbing a currently unknown anomaly, which\ eventually would evolve to become the Fly of the Grayed Flowers, which left the place and began living as a nomad. )/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Arial 8 Tf)/DS(font: Arial,sans-serif 8.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240920191311-03'00')/NM(d7acb930cdb148c288da8a71ac95f1c3)/Page 1/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal\;font-family:Arial;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:justify">Localized on the suburban area of Compelvista, a short walk of the Golden Oasis Shopping Center, the 3-flower hotel Radiant Resting boasts it&#8217;s 7 floors, with 8 ro\oms each. The hotel is great for visitors from home and overseas alike, with its deluxe brutalist architecture, its typical appeal for tourists and the convenience of its close placement to the shopping center being great positives, although countered by \their &#8220;distinct&#8221; prices. Usually operating in a 24h fashion with the most luxurious room service in the whole city, the hotel is plagued with an anomaly in its structure, that takes the form of one of its rooms on the 4</span><span style="text\-align:justify;vertical-align:+0.0pt">th</span><span style="text-align:justify"> floor, room 409. The entity that resides in this room consists of a multidimensional structure-like parasite, that infects buildings and slowly substitutes it, with its final\ stage being a target structure&#8217;s copy, spatially connected to a kind of hivemind in an undetermined size liminal space. A secondary characteristic of the parasite consists in consuming the target structure with vines and plants until they reach a r\uin-like state. These plants are active and can be hostile to humans, despite not being very strong. The place can also consciously change its formation as a tactic to confuse invaders and remove any escape routes. In the hotel&#8217;s case, this specific\ iteration of the entity had a stunted development, becoming completely unable to expand beyond room 409, and creating a replica of the bathroom of room 404 as a facade, leading to guests thinking that the room was only an employee bathroom, no longer in \use, and avoiding further investigation. Its door is identical to the other ones on the floor, with the only difference being its number, 409, the only of the kind in all of the building. The plants inside are the main method of propagation, sticking the \spores on clothing or skin of invaders that later detach in other places. The room 409 iteration, though, cannot produce spores, as its biology was permanently altered after absorbing a currently unknown anomaly, which eventually would evolve to become th\e Fly of the Grayed Flowers, which left the place and began living as a nomad. </span></p></body>)/Rect[45.3301 61.054 571.322 206.874]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj90 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(   Dif)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg 0 Tc 0 Tw 100 Tz 0 TL 0 Ts 0 Tr /Helv 21.8 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 21.8pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240914153110-03'00')/NM(1136aaeffc294a48afa27816b1ee9af3)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:21.8pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">   Dif</span></p></body>)/Rect[17.301 674.202 180.873 699.612]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj91 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(   Dif)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg 0 Tc 0 Tw 100 Tz 0 TL 0 Ts 0 Tr /Helv 21.8 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 21.8pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240915090221-03'00')/NM(0c0217f3efab44cfa7436d40591ae631)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:2