color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">Restrict - In case the strategy change into immobilizing the target, it can use the plants around the room to capture some parts of the target's body,\ or completely encase it in a plant coccoon, or, in rare occasions, can move said &quot;rooms' to confuse or separate them.</span></p></body>)/Rect[181.528 571.32 517.093 623.854]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj102 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(Parasitic Spores \(ÿ\) - Uses some of the plants to release a spore cloud which can cause diverse effects in the targets, from poisoning them on 1% Dif CS Damage per turn, causing hallucinations, which reduce the Target's Property values in 13 if organic \and compatible, and also being a common form of reproduction. On this sheet, the Gear is blocked while the targets are in the area equivalent to the hotel's surroundings. )/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 8 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 8.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240920192850-03'00')/NM(0b13cda8c8ee498badf7f34d2c2a2f89)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal\;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">Parasitic Spores \(</span><span style="font-weight:bold;font-family:Arial">&#216;</span><span style="font-family:Helvetica">\) - Uses some of the plant\s to release a spore cloud which can cause diverse effects in the targets, from poisoning them on 1% Dif CS Damage per turn, causing hallucinations, which reduce the Target's Property values in 13 if organic and compatible, and also being a common form of\ reproduction. On this sheet, the Gear is blocked while the targets are in the area equivalent to the hotel's surroundings. </span></p></body>)/Rect[181.528 475.919 518.402 531.582]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj103 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(Lurk - As it is practically the whole battle area, it can take advantage of that entering a lurking mode by using this Gear, gaining an opening to cammouflage, retract itself from the room, confuse the opponent using objects on the room, or even marking t\hem with an annoying signal.)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 9 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 9.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240920193028-03'00')/NM(4ad9b17ed327424288eb2d55c9c580e4)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal\;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">Lurk - As it is practically the whole battle area, it can take advantage of that entering a lurking mode by using this Gear, gaining an opening to camm\ouflage, retract itself from the room, confuse the opponent using objects on the room, or even marking them with an annoying signal.</span></p></body>)/Rect[182.183 299.997 515.13 354.747]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj104 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(Absorption - When leaving a target vulnerable \(Destroying all of its Gear, Severing the Property/Essence Link...\) can use this Gear to eat it and end the fight.)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 10 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 10.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240920192257-03'00')/NM(e5d6d6beb785412c93a0ea2c110921d7)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.